// `list_member` is the sanctioned custom-equality membership, not `std.algebra.contains`: the seed
// intercepts `contains` and discards its `eq` argument (declared at `std.list`'s own header, tracked by
// `gunbc.list_membership_operation_gap`), so `contains(xs:, item:, eq:)` silently falls back to whole-
// struct structural equality. Dedup here compares `KnownRedSubject`s whose `origin` differs between the
// wet schedule and the roster, so that fallback never collapsed a dual-membership identity and a claim
// enrolled AND scheduled was dispatched twice. `list_member` runs `xs.any`, which does honour its
// predicate, so the comparison below is the one actually executed.
